      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary artery bypass surgery has a survival rate of 98 to 99 per cent. Recent statistics demonstrate that it offers an increased life span and long term relief (or improvement) of symptoms; the efficacy of surgery is proven, especially in those with left main and multiple coronary vessel disease. For most patients the indications for referral are clear; for some they are not. Risk factors (before and after surgery) must be reduced."},
